      "FacilityID": 1000121548,
      "SummaryText": "Ag Plus Cooperative\n1512 State Highway 19\nHendricks MN 56136\n\nFor further information contact Keith Pillatzki, Location Manager, at 507-694-1197\nA) The Facility Policy\nThe owners, management and employees of Ag Plus Cooperative are committed to the prevention of any accidental release of anhydrous ammonia.  If any accidental release should occur, the facility is prepared to work with the local fire department or other authorities to mitigate any release and minimize the impact of the release to people and the environment.\nB) Facility Information\nThe primary activity at the facility is the storage and distribution of fertilizer to farmers.\nAnhydrous ammonia, used for crop production nutrients, is received, stored and distributed for direct application to soil.\nC) The accidental release prevention program\nThe facility has implemented the provision of Safety Requirements for the Storage and Handling of Anhydrous Ammonia, K-61.1, published by the American National Standards Institute, Inc. and the Standards of the U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration, 29 CFR 1910.111, Storage and Handling of Anhydrous Ammonia, as well as the requirements of the Minnesota Department of Agriculture Rules.\nD) The five year accident history\nThere have been no accidental releases of anhydrous ammonia in the past five years that have caused any deaths, injuries, or significant property damage at the facility.\n\nE) The emergency response program\nThe facility has:\n1)\tA written emergency action plan, in accordance with OSHA standard, 29 CFR 1910.38;\n2)\tProvided state and local authorities with the emergency planning and community right to know information as required under SARA Title III;\n3)\tCoordinated with local emergency responders and the fire department.\n\nF) Planned changes to improve safety\nSafety improvement is an ongoing process at the facility.  Periodic evaluations as required by state and federal law are performed to assess the condition of equipment and processes and imp"
    },
